# Third-party binaries (ffmpeg, MakeMKV, HandBrake), the embedded
# Python runtime, downloaded alert sounds and run logs stay local. The
# settings point at sounds/, so the paths are in the repo and the audio
# is not - publishing somebody else's music is not this repo's business.

tools/
sounds/
python/
logs/
# quieter copies of the alert sounds, rendered on demand from files
# that are not in here either
soundcache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
# Real disc fragments kept as test fixtures - see .testdata/README.md.
# Small, but still disc content, so they stay out of the repo.
.testdata/
config.toml.bak

# The live config and the drive's own journal are per-machine state. config.toml
# carries an out_dir with somebody's username in it; dead-sectors.json is keyed
# by disc label and sector count, so a shared copy hands a stranger a standing
# refusal to read sectors of their own film. Both are created at runtime;
# config.example.toml is the one that ships.
config.toml
dead-sectors.json
# Agent skills, not project source.
.claude/
